    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 11.2</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="11.2" corresp="#wit-hk">De l'ungle, s'il le couped de la charn, V sol. de souz Engleis. A l'ungle del petit dei, IIII den.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk">For the nail if it is cut away from the flesh, 5 English shillings [shall be paid], and for the nail of the little finger 4 pence.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="501"><ref target="clause:Af_56-1">Af 56.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:Af_60">Af 60</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 56, 1 | ebd. 60</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 258–259 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
